# Use strong models for hard work

- For hard tasks (model training design, debugging tricky results, deep code/research reviews, architecture decisions), delegate to subagents on the strongest available model. Don't default to cheap/fast models to save cost.
- Pick the latest top-tier model from the available list (e.g., latest Claude Opus thinking-high or latest GPT); use fast models only for simple lookups.
- Say which model was used and for what.
- Note: the agent cannot change the main chat model; the user picks that in Cursor.
